and left eyes</article-title><source>J Allergy Clin Immunol</source><volume>92</volume><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8335854</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b6-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Als-Nielsen</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Gluud</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Association of funding and conclusions in randomized drug trials</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>290</volume><fpage>921</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12928469</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="web"><collab>American College of Physicians Observer</collab><year>2004</year><source>President&#x02019;s Column: Heeding the public&#x02019;s call for better quality and safety [online]</source><date-in-citation>Accessed 25 September 2007</date-in-citation><comment>URL: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.acponline.org/journals/news/sep04/president.htm">http://www.acponline.org/journals/news/sep04/president.htm</ext-link></comment></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amiel</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Moreau</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Vincent-Genod</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Noninvitation of eligible individuals to participate in pediatric studies: a qualitative study</article-title><source>Arch Pediatr Adolesc Med</source><volume>161</volume><fpage>446</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17485619</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arevalo</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Fromow-Guerra</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Quiroz-Mercado</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Primary intravitreal bevacizumab (avastin) for diabetic macular edema: results from the pan-American collaborative retina study group at 6-month follow-up</article-title><source>Ophthalmol</source><volume>114</volume><fpage>743</fpage><lpage>50</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Armitage</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Colton</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><source>Encyclopedia of biostatistics</source><publisher-loc>Hoboken NJ, USA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>John Wiley and Sons, Inc</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barton</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Using clinical evidence</article-title><source>BMJ</source><volume>322</volume><fpage>503</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11230051</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beck</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Cleary</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><collab>for The Optic Neuritis Study Group</collab><year>1992</year><article-title>A randomized, controlled trial of corticosteroids in the treatment of acute optic neuritis</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><volume>326</volume><fpage>581</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1734247</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beck</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Sample size for a clinical trial: why do some trials need only 100 patients and others 1000 patients or more?</article-title><source>Ophthalmol</source><volume>113</volume><fpage>721</fpage><lpage>2</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benatar</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Heparin use in acute ischaemic stroke: does evidence change practice?</article-title><source>Q J Med</source><volume>98</volume><fpage>147</fpage><lpage>52</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berdy</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Stoppel</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name><name><surname>Epstein</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Comparison of the clinical efficacy and tolerability of olopatadine hydrochloride 0.1% ophthalmic solution and loteprednol etabonate 0.2% ophthalmic suspension in the conjunctival allergen challenge model</article-title><source>Clin Ther</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>918</fpage><lpage>29</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12117082</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-co-2-401"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bresalier</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Sandler</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Quan</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person